   "id": "H_shard0_raw_mip_inner_core",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "✗ **H_shard0_raw_mip_inner_core** · hypothesis\n\nDirect 2D (Z, s) unrolling from shard_0 phase crossings (abs_w = 16..6, snapped along normal rs to the Lasagna_cos ridge) with uncancelled raw 3D MIP ink sampling (student-v12A + v3-78k) will expose ink signal in the inner core\n\n*why dead:* [L-PT-003=0] Geometric 2D (Z,s) unrolling from shard_0 (seed_w=13,10) + Lasagna_cos normal snapping + L4 GPU 4-model inference succeeded (ens4>100 peaked 4.5x at dn=0: 24.8% vs 5.5%/6.1% at dn=+-18), but Thin-Sheet Z-DoG and CT relief prove activations on 5753_-7..-14 are horizontal delamination ridges and flat-face reed fibers, with 0 legible Greek title letters (X11)",
